            "text": "<p>Most fabric bibs are water-resistant at best \u2014 a surface treatment that wears off after a few washes. When blueberry juice or tomato sauce hits, it soaks through to the outfit underneath. You're still doing a full change.</p><p>The Loulou Lollipop long sleeve bib uses a <strong>waterproof TPU-sealed backing</strong> on the front panel and both sleeves. That's a physical barrier, not a coating. Tested across full-strength tomato sauce, beet juice, and yogurt \u2014 none of it bleeds through. The bib takes the hit. The outfit doesn't.</p>",
